  "expertText": "* = $0801\n; MOUSE macro demo - sprite#0 follows a C64 1351 mouse on port 1. VICE: Settings > Input > Control Port 1 > Mouse (1351)\n; Init: select port 1 via CIA bits 7:6 (%01xxxxxx), then store raw POT samples in $FD/$FE\n.region Init\n    JMP main\n.align 64\n.byte $C0,$00,$00,$E0,$00,$00,$F0,$00,$00,$D8,$00,$00,$CC,$00,$00,$C6,$00,$00,$C3,$00,$00,$C1,$80,$00,$C0,$C0,$00,$C0,$60,$00,$C0,$30,$00,$C0,$18,$00,$C3,$FC,$00,$C6,$00,$00,$CC,$00,$00,$F8,$00,$00,$F0,$00,$00,$C0,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00\n.endregion \n\n.region Main\nmain:\n    SEI\n    JSR $E544\n.text 15, 0, \"MOUSE DEMO\"\n.text 6, 2, \"MOVE A 1351 MOUSE ON PORT 1\"\n.text 3, 3, \"SPRITE TRACKS SID POTX/POTY DELTA\"\n.sprite_init 0, 1, $21\n.sprite_pos 0, 152, 100\n    LDA $DC00\n    AND #$3F\n    ORA #$40\n    STA $DC00\n    LDA $D419\n    STA $FD\n    LDA $D41A\n    STA $FE\ngameloop:\n.wait_raster $F8\n.mouse 1, 0, FD, FE\n.mouse 1, 0, FD, FE\n    JMP gameloop\n.endregion ",
